## File Formats

Each element directory contains two files:
- **README.md** — static description (what the element is, scope, acceptance criteria). Does not change during execution.
- **progress.md** — dynamic lifecycle journal (status, Task/Bug estimate, assignment, timestamps, dependencies, checklist, notes). Updated throughout execution.

Both files use source-aware, injection-safe Markdown persistence. Unchanged
bytes and custom sections are retained during rewrites; free-text payload fields
round-trip byte-exact. Mutation boundaries normalize identifier-like fields
(`AssignedTo`, `BlockedBy`, `Blocks`) by trimming boundary whitespace and reject
empty or reserved `(none)` values with a typed error. Checklist text is rejected
only when empty-after-trim and is otherwise persisted verbatim.

Task/bug dependencies are bidirectional ground truth. Story/epic ordering is derived from the live task DAG at read time; task links never materialize container side-effect links. Explicit stored container links remain manual state, while projections expose task-derived blockers separately.

For detailed format specifications, field descriptions, and examples, see [`references/file-formats.md`](references/file-formats.md).

